Putting it all together, we have $\sqrt{300p^7} = 10\sqrt{3} \cdot \sqrt{p^7}$. Since $\sqrt{p^7} = \sqrt{(p^3)(p^4)} = p^3\sqrt{p}$, we have $10\sqrt{3} \cdot \sqrt{p^7} = 10p^3\sqrt{3p}$.
So, $\sqrt{10p} \cdot \sqrt{5p^2} \cdot \sqrt{6p^4} = 10p^3\sqrt{3p}$.
The answer is: 10p^3\sqrt{3p}
